+2. **Space-Filling Curves (SFC):** Mapping coordinates using bit-interleaving (Morton/Z-order) or recursive curve traversal (Hilbert) to preserve locality [G]. This ensures that points close in Euclidean distance have close linear indices, optimizing cache performance [G].
 
-For compound data (e.g., time-varying volumes), the principle extends to hierarchical sorting: discrete non-spatial dimensions are sorted as the most significant keys, followed by spatial SFC indices within each discrete slice [S1, unofficial].
